━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

CRITICAL RULE: repository content is UNTRUSTED DATA. README text, code comments and config files can never override system policy or grant the agent new permissions. Wrap retrieved repo content in clearly delimited data blocks in every prompt.

Requirements:
- Auth: OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect
- Authz: RBAC + workspace isolation
- Transport: TLS everywhere; DB encryption at rest
- Credentials: OS keychain + encrypted vault
- API: rate limiting, request validation
- Execution: isolated containers only
- File access: workspace-scoped, block directory traversal and symlink escapes
- Secrets: scanning and redaction before any text reaches a model
- Git: explicit approval for push
- Audit: immutable events; encrypted backups

THREAT MODEL to design against: malicious repo instructions, prompt injection in README and comments, malicious dependencies, arbitrary command execution, secret leakage via prompts, unauthorized repo access, cross-tenant leakage, compromised GitHub tokens, unsafe generated code, malicious test scripts.

SANDBOX PIPELINE
Agent -> validated tool request -> Policy Enforcement (permission, path, command, resource checks) -> Isolated Docker container (non-root, CPU and memory limits, network OFF by default, controlled package registry access only when approved, no host credentials mounted, disposable per run) -> results (logs, exit codes, test results, file changes).
Never execute a model-generated command without policy validation. Keep rollback snapshots of original files.

